Before adopting new Azure workloads, organisations should evaluate whether people, processes, and technology are prepared for cloud operations.

A readiness assessment may include:

* Technical skills
* Governance framework
* Security controls
* Network readiness
* Compliance requirements
* Budget planning
* Operational support model

For example, an organisation may postpone a migration until administrators complete Azure training and monitoring processes are fully established.

A real-life use case is reducing migration failures through better preparation.

Cloud readiness assessments improve planning accuracy and project success.
